Z||000000||4Banger Bandit||08-18-99||06:34 PM||||Hey guys, I'm getting an 87 GT Auto from a repairables lot in a couple days.  The only damage to it is a torn and buckled nose, two ripped front fenders and a thrashed hood.  The cool part is, I've already got another fiero with a new GT nose, hood, and fenders that will work nicely.  How hard is it to swap fenders???? I'd really appreciate your advice.  The car is near-mint everywhere else, including the interior.  It's maroon and silver with a sunroof, all power, nice tires, automatic.  I started the car up, and it purrs like a kitten.  The tranny seems to be in good shape too.  It just has a little bit of what sounds like a vacuum leak.  It idles on it's own just fine, but just slightly erratic. Any ideas? Itsounds soooooo much cooler than my 4banger!! He wanted 2,300 for it, but I got him down to 2,000 even. All I need to do is swap some front end pieces, paint them, and it's like new.  what do you think???
