Z||000013||theogre||08-20-99||12:56 AM||||well........... run the calculator for yourself........... fiero "book" values for 87 GT in decent shape are pretty high. Higher frankly than I expected. ((I'm looking at an 86 GT myself.....))<p>check the used car guide here. I've checked. It's in line with NADA and other books.<p> <A HREF="http://www.autosite.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autosite.com/</A> <p>You do need to lean on a scrapper..... they don't have shit into the car. The so called "repairable" lot isn't any differant.<p>This clown wants 3K$ for an 86 GT.... No F#$%ing way. It needs brakes. has a shitty repaint. needs engine work. (valve guides at the very least are gone...... Vac lines are all hosed........ Was suprised it ran as well as it did.)
