Z||000016||peabody||08-21-99||09:40 AM||||Hey, guys, he's asking about swapping the fenders, not if you think he got screwed on the damaged GT. A fender repair is fairly easy. Just unscrew everything that looks bolted on. The lower part of the fender is attached behind the rocker covers. The "pop rivets" that hold the rocker covers have to be drilled off. They're under the rectangular covers in the top of the rocker covers. Also its attached from underneath. Just remove as many as are needed to give you access to the bottom fender rivets. It's easier to sand and paint prior to putting on the car. Hope this helps. 
